  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0895f7676762ba444b808767ad362585, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The university archive. I was pulling first editions before the dust reaches them. Then my ethics lecture, on schedule.
    midDaysAnswer: The university. The lab wing has cracked and the dean wants a report. I still lectured. Eleven students came.
    finalDaysAnswer: The faculty building. Empty halls. I left my lecture notes on the desk. There is no reason to carry them now.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The chemistry laboratory. I teach organic chemistry. Fifteen years in the same department.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My flat. I cancelled all lectures weeks ago. Routine is a comfort for the unreflective.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Faculty housing. I live alone. I never married, and I consider it the soundest decision I made.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Headaches, occasionally. I have always had them. Nothing that requires the polyclinic.
    midDaysAnswer: I lose track of time. I look up from a book and it is dark. The headaches come more often.
    finalDaysAnswer: A taste of copper in the mouth. Two weeks now. I find I no longer mind it.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: None. I have never had a headache in my life. A disciplined mind does not permit it.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Nothing. At twenty-eight one still recovers quickly. I sleep well and wake rested.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing. I resigned from the university last year for my health, and it has improved since.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Stoicism is the only logical response to a crisis. Would you not agree?
    - My students keep asking me what comes next. I tell them what history says. They do not like the answer.
    - Order is its own kind of courage, officer. You are practicing it right now.
    midDays:
    - Human intellect is a very fragile glass, and the hammer is coming.
    - I gave a lecture to an empty hall yesterday. I finished it. Habit is the skeleton of civilization.
    - The books are starting to feel heavy. As if the ink itself is rotting.
    finalDays:
    - Why check the papers? Soon the ash will be the only record anyone keeps.
    - The fire is a beautiful editor. It deletes all our mistakes at once.
    - Zero is the only honest number in a collapsing system. Everything reduces to it.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
